# November 23, 2026: a second scatter of places across South Carolina, filling ground the first two batches left empty:
# York, Chester and Lancaster counties in the north, Newberry and Abbeville in the west, Anderson (Pendleton), Sumter
# (Stateburg), Horry (Conway and Bucksville), Georgetown (the Santee), Charleston city and the Ashley River, Colleton
# (Jacksonboro) and Bamberg (Rivers Bridge). Region sc claimed with choose.py --thinnest (36 places, the fewest of any).
# Facts come only from sources opened in this session: Wikipedia read as raw text, HMdb marker texts (Pon Pon Chapel),
# and the pages of South Carolina State Parks, Drayton Hall, the Old Exchange, the Culture & Heritage Museums
# (Brattonsville), the Newberry Opera House, the Pendleton Historic Foundation, Hopsewee, the state tourism office
# (Burt-Stark Mansion) and the Charleston City Paper (Powder Magazine closing, March 2025).
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
